1
00:01:17,689 --> 00:01:19,205
The bakery opens at six every morning.

2
00:01:22,926 --> 00:01:26,536
Mara lights the oven
before the sun comes up.

3
00:01:27,788 --> 00:01:30,399
The first train leaves the
station at half past six.

4
00:01:30,825 --> 00:01:32,511
Can I have two rolls and a coffee, please?

5
00:01:35,222 --> 00:01:38,970
Of course. Do you want milk with it?

6
00:01:39,968 --> 00:01:43,467
Just a little, thank you.

7
00:01:45,169 --> 00:01:48,170
The weather report says rain after lunch.

8
00:03:03,396 --> 00:03:05,374
Then I will take the umbrella today.

9
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:08,920
The train to the coast
is ten minutes late.

10
00:03:12,838 --> 00:03:15,380
That happens every Tuesday.

11
00:03:18,793 --> 00:03:20,569
The flour delivery comes at eight.

12
00:03:23,659 --> 00:03:27,694
Please put the sacks
next to the back door.

13
00:03:29,345 --> 00:03:31,224
How many loaves do we need for the market?

14
00:03:31,899 --> 00:03:33,574
Forty, and twenty small ones.

15
00:04:00,510 --> 00:04:03,677
The wind is getting stronger.

16
00:04:07,211 --> 00:04:09,260
Close the window, the
papers are flying around.

17
00:04:13,003 --> 00:04:14,756
Is the platform for the
north line still closed?

18
00:04:16,907 --> 00:04:20,566
Yes, they repair the tracks until Friday.

19
00:04:24,202 --> 00:04:28,413
Then I take the bus to the next station.

20
00:04:32,243 --> 00:04:33,716
The bus leaves from the square at nine.

21
00:04:37,219 --> 00:04:38,424
Do you have any rye bread left?

22
00:05:20,230 --> 00:05:22,634
Only one loaf, but it is fresh.

23
00:05:24,533 --> 00:05:26,017
I will take it.

24
00:05:27,830 --> 00:05:31,267
That is three euros fifty.

25
00:05:34,046 --> 00:05:35,267
The clouds look darker now.

26
00:05:38,512 --> 00:05:40,748
Bring the chairs inside
before the rain starts.

27
00:05:43,044 --> 00:05:45,244
The conductor checks the tickets twice.

28
00:05:48,029 --> 00:05:50,893
I lost my ticket
somewhere on the platform.

29
00:09:39,717 --> 00:09:41,104
You can buy a new one on the train.

30
00:09:42,874 --> 00:09:47,328
The oven needs a new door seal.

31
00:09:47,711 --> 00:09:49,267
I will call the repair shop tomorrow.

32
00:09:52,232 --> 00:09:56,667
It is snowing in the mountains already.

33
00:09:57,279 --> 00:09:59,107
The pass road is closed for trucks.

34
00:10:01,970 --> 00:10:04,854
The night train still runs on time.

35
00:10:08,583 --> 00:10:10,198
We sell more cake when it rains.

36
00:10:22,799 --> 00:10:24,675
People want something warm with their tea.

37
00:10:26,557 --> 00:10:28,551
The station clock is five minutes fast.

38
00:10:30,638 --> 00:10:32,133
Nobody has fixed it since spring.

39
00:10:34,576 --> 00:10:36,806
Can you take the early shift on Saturday?

40
00:10:37,922 --> 00:10:39,608
Yes, but I need to leave at noon.

41
00:10:41,075 --> 00:10:43,257
The sun is back in the afternoon.

42
00:10:47,168 --> 00:10:50,532
The market square is full again.

43
00:12:08,432 --> 00:12:11,210
Two coffees and an apple cake, please.

44
00:12:11,850 --> 00:12:15,125
Sit by the window, the view is nice.

45
00:12:18,159 --> 00:12:22,609
The last train goes at eleven.

46
00:12:22,934 --> 00:12:24,255
Do not miss it, the next one is at five.

47
00:12:27,467 --> 00:12:29,439
The bakery closes at seven in the evening.

48
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:31,230
Mara cleans the counters
and counts the money.

49
00:12:34,516 --> 00:12:37,500
Tomorrow the forecast says frost.

50
00:14:00,459 --> 00:14:04,219
Then the dough needs more time to rise.

51
00:14:06,301 --> 00:14:08,648
The station master waves the green flag.

52
00:14:10,225 --> 00:14:11,978
The train pulls out slowly.

53
00:14:15,699 --> 00:14:18,244
Good night, see you at six.

54
00:14:20,295 --> 00:14:22,841
Good night, and do not forget the keys.

55
00:14:25,160 --> 00:14:29,178
The street lights come on one by one.

56
00:14:31,877 --> 00:14:34,699
A cat sleeps on the
warm step of the bakery.

57
00:15:35,936 --> 00:15:39,675
The first frost covers the tracks.

58
00:15:42,230 --> 00:15:45,184
The morning train is full of students.

59
00:15:46,192 --> 00:15:47,890
Mara opens the door and the bell rings.

60
00:15:50,651 --> 00:15:54,214
Good morning, the usual please.
